From 0005-gmux-i915-switcheroo Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0005/0005] drm/i915: retry eDP DPCD probe to cover gmux AUX
 power-up race

On dual GPU MacBook Pros (retina, pre-T2) the eDP AUX channel is routed
through the gmux eDP mux, which cannot switch AUX separately from the
main link. When the panel mux has just been switched to this GPU - e.g.
booting with the integrated GPU primary after gpu-switch -i, or after a
vga_switcheroo reprobe - the panel power sequencer / gmux may not have
the AUX channel stable yet during the initial DPCD read.

Today intel_edp_init_dpcd() performs exactly one
drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps(). If it fails, the eDP connector is permanently
disabled as a ghost:

    [ENCODER:%d:%s] failed to retrieve link info, disabling eDP

Add a short retry loop (5 attempts, 50 ms apart) around the initial
DPCD read so a transient power-up race does not brick the panel until
the next boot.

This does not help the *reverse* case (panel muxed to the discrete GPU
while i915 is bound): there the AUX channel is physically routed to the
other GPU and no retry can make it respond - that is expected and still
results in a disabled eDP connector on the inactive GPU.

VBT/OpRegion: on Haswell the panel VBT data is consumed by
intel_bios_init_panel_early() from the ACPI OpRegion. Whether a VBT is
present on this specific board could not be verified read-only (needs an
acpidump/sysfs check at runtime); i915 can operate with EDID/DPCD-only
panel info if the VBT is absent, so this is not a blocker for the retry.

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git i/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c w/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
index 113d767e6..8eae7a178 100644
--- i/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
+++ w/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c
@@ -4770,12 +4770,29 @@ static bool
 intel_edp_init_dpcd(struct intel_dp *intel_dp, struct intel_connector *connector)
 {
 	struct intel_display *display = to_intel_display(intel_dp);
+	int i;
 	int ret;

 	/* this function is meant to be called only once */
 	drm_WARN_ON(display->drm, intel_dp->dpcd[DP_DPCD_REV] != 0);

-	if (drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps(&intel_dp->aux, intel_dp->dpcd) != 0)
+	/*
+	 * On dual GPU MacBook Pros the eDP AUX channel is routed through the
+	 * gmux. When the panel mux has just been switched to this GPU (e.g.
+	 * booting with the integrated GPU primary after gpu-switch -i, or a
+	 * vga_switcheroo reprobe), the panel power sequencer / gmux may not
+	 * have the AUX channel stable yet. Retry the initial DPCD read a few
+	 * times before giving up, otherwise the connector is permanently
+	 * disabled as a "ghost" ("failed to retrieve link info, disabling
+	 * eDP") on a transient power-up race.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
+		ret = drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps(&intel_dp->aux, intel_dp->dpcd);
+		if (ret == 0)
+			break;
+		msleep(50);
+	}
+	if (ret != 0)
 		return false;

 	drm_dp_read_desc(&intel_dp->aux, &intel_dp->desc,
--
